cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these bounds or this verification code, please cite it."
title: "Kissing numbers: new lower bounds in dimensions 18 through 96, with verification packages"
abstract: >-
  Verification packages for constructive kissing-number lower bounds in 70
  dimensions: 18, 25-46, 49-71 and 73-96. The synchronized 28 October 2026
  registry gives 201136, 209600, 221694, 231638, 247960 and 251110 in
  dimensions 26-31, improving the pinned PackingStar configurations by
  2, 14, 30, 2, 4 and 108 points. Complete exact coordinate checks include
  every unpaired point in the asymmetric constructions. Concurrent results
  include 611522 in 38D, 2919782 in 43D and 142162362560 in 96D.
  The nonlinear (96,2^37,24) parent code is prior work of Duursma,
  Greferath, Litsyn and Schmidt (2001); sparse additions and exact central
  sections are documented separately from that published dense-code gain.
  Packages state their exact arithmetic, independent replays and inherited
  inputs. These are lower bounds without unrestricted optimality claims.
  The paper and PDF retain their earlier 66-result checkpoint; pending
  dimensions and improvements are listed in common/manuscript_scope.json.
authors:
